WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:10.181
Three companies — Rogers, Bell, and TELUS — control eighty-seven percent of Canadian wireless revenue, charging among the highest prices in the developed world.

00:00:10.181 --> 00:00:16.318
The CRTC, the regulator meant to protect Canadians, has been captured by the industry it oversees.

00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:25.556
And when a fourth competitor proved that twenty-five dollar plans were commercially viable, the Big Three simply matched them — revealing the profit margin was always there.

00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:30.829
Canadians have been paying oligopoly prices for decades, and the regulator did nothing.
